EDIT: app/src/manifest.ts
```
<<<<<<< SEARCH
        out.push(`Amendments: ${notes.length}`);
=======
        out.push(`Amendments: ${notes.length}`);
        const latest = notes[notes.length - 1];
        out.push(`Latest: ${latest.text} (${latest.by})`);
>>>>>>> REPLACE
```

I added the "Latest:" line right after the "Amendments:" count line in `renderManifest`. It sits inside the existing `notes.length > 0` block, so sheets with no amendments are unchanged.

I couldn't see the body of `amend` or `amendments()`, so I assumed `amendments()` returns them oldest-first and the most recent is the last one. If it returns them newest-first or sorted some other way, change the index to `notes[0]`.
